text:
tara: opened PR #556 to introduce a validator-friendly tool-calling shape and a tiny migration guide: https://github.com/redwood-inference/docs/pull/556

evan: nice! can we include a compact, copy-paste JSON Schema + a short parsing snippet for Rust? a lot of infra teams are experimenting with Rust.

morgan: agree on Rust. also request: show both named-arg (object) and positional-arg (array) examples, and add `additionalProperties: false` so validators catch typos quickly.

alina: heads-up 1 docs still reference `function_call` and `tool_name`. we should standardize on `tool` in all examples and include a one-line backward-compat mapping.

tara: sketching a minimal schema here (validator-oriented). copy/paste friendly:```json
{
  "type": "object",
  "properties": {
    "tool": {"type": "string"},
    "args": {
      "oneOf": [
        {"type": "object"},
        {"type": "array"}
      ]
    },
    "meta": {"type": "object"},
    "confidence": {"type": "number", "minimum": 0, "maximum": 1}
  },
  "required": ["tool", "args"],
  "additionalProperties": false
}
```

evan: ok. for concrete validator patterns, add an enum example for common tools (web_fetch, kv_get) so teams can tighten schemas per tool.

morgan: paste that variant so we can include it directly:```json
{
  "type": "object",
  "properties": {
    "tool": {"type": "string", "enum": ["web_fetch", "kv_get"]},
    "args": {
      "oneOf": [
        {"type": "object", "properties": {"url": {"type": "string"}}, "required": ["url"]},
        {"type": "array"}
      ]
    }
  },
  "required": ["tool", "args"],
  "additionalProperties": false
}
```

alina: please add the compatibility mapping sentence: "Legacy: map `function_call.name` -> `tool` and `function_call.arguments` -> `args` (object or array)." Put it in a highlighted note.

tara: done. adding a Rust parse example too (very small):```rust
use serde_json::Value;

let out = client.generate(...).await?;
let parsed: Value = serde_json::from_str(&out.output)?;
let tool = parsed.get("tool").and_then(|v| v.as_str()).unwrap_or("");
match tool {
  "web_fetch" => {
    let args = parsed.get("args").unwrap();
    let url = args.get("url").and_then(|v| v.as_str()).unwrap();
    fetch(url).await;
  }
  _ => (),
}
```

evan: excellent. also add a short note that `confidence` is advisory only and not a calibrated probability. link to /guides/evals for guidance.

morgan: snippet linter flagged an internal link in the migration doc: it pointed to `/sdk/py/old-tooling`. that will 404 for external customers. tara, can you replace with `/sdk/python/migration#tool-calls` and open a redirect for the old path? marketing asked us to add redirects for any public path we change.

tara: yup i'll swap the path and open a tiny `_redirects.yml` PR for the old endpoint, tag marketing.

ci-bot: CI: docs lint + snippet-check for PR #556  4 files changed, 21 insertions(+), 9 deletions(-)  https://ci.internal/redwood/556 :white_check_mark:

evan: final reviewer? i can take one last pass tomorrow morning. also suggest adding a 1-line migration checklist at the top of the doc so teams can scan quickly.

tara: good idea, i'll add a 3-item checklist: 1) update examples to `tool`/`args`, 2) apply enum schemas per tool if needed, 3) add redirect for old SDK paths. will push shortly and ping for review.

morgan: thanks all. small ask from me 1 include an explicit example showing positional args array usage for a `kv_get` call (e.g., "args": ["my-key"]). makes it easier for readers.

tara: added that snippet in the examples section. aiming to merge by EOD. thanks everyone :shipit:
